<title>USA: U.S. Republicans to cut taxes $163 bln in 5 years.</title>
<headline>U.S. Republicans to cut taxes $163 bln in 5 years.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Senate Majority Leader Trent Lott outlined a Republican agenda for this session of Congress that includes legislation to reduce taxes by $163 billion over five years, including a capital gains tax cut.</p>
<p>The Republican legislation, would create a $500 per child tax credit for children under the age of 18. It would raise the contribution limit for spousal, tax-deferred individual retirement accounts to $2,000 from the current $250.</p>
</text>
